## Run it

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

The site opens at `http://localhost:<%= port %>`.

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Dev server |
| `npm run build` | Static build in `dist/`<%= layers.search ? ', with the search index' : '' %> |
| `npm run preview` | Serves the build |
| `npm run verify` | `link-loom check`, `astro check` and the build: run it before every push |
| `npm run gen:images` | Generates image masters from `images.manifest.json` (needs `link-loom services add image-generation`) |
| `npm run optimize:images` | Turns the masters into WebP in `public/images` |
| `npm run og:compose` | Composes a page's share image in the brand: `npm run og:compose -- "Pricing"` |
| `npm run version-patch` | Bumps the patch version, tags it and pushes the tag |

## Add to it

Use the CLI so every piece follows the same standard:

```bash
npx link-loom describe --project
npx link-loom add page --path /company --title-en Company --title-es Compañía --nav footer:company
npx link-loom add section --page home --kind cards --id benefits
```

## Deploy

`npm run build` writes a static site to `dist/`; any static host serves it. On Cloudflare Pages:
`npx wrangler pages deploy dist --project-name=<%= slug %>`. `public/_redirects` sends `/` to `/<%= defaultLocale %>/`.
